  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Sanary-sur-Mer, between Bandol and Six-Fours-les-Plages, has a very central marina lined by the market and pedestrian lanes. Two of its hotels publish clear dog rules on their own websites; a third, often listed as pet-friendly, actually refuses animals.</p>

      <h2>Adonis Sanary – Grand Hôtel des Bains (3 stars)</h2>
      <p>At 25 boulevard d'Estienne d'Orves, close to the market and the harbour, the Adonis has 31 rooms on two floors and a large garden. Its website states: pets €10 per animal per day, dogs under 10 kg only, "dogs over 10 kg will be refused"; the Sanary tourist office lists the same rule in its 2026 rates. Reception 7am-9pm, check-in 3pm, check-out 11am, private parking €18/day subject to availability, buffet breakfast €15 (7:30-10am), tourist tax €2.45 per person per day. Only the accessible room is on the ground floor; the others are reached by stairs. Phone: +33 4 94 74 13 47.</p>

      <h2>Hostellerie La Farandole (4 stars)</h2>
      <p>At 140 chemin de la Plage, on the sandy Gorguette beach facing the bay of Bandol, with direct beach access, three restaurants, a spa, an outdoor pool heated from May to September, and paid underground or free outdoor parking. Its website states: "Pets allowed with a supplement of €30 per animal per night", with no published weight limit. Check-in from 3pm, check-out 11am. Phone: +33 4 94 90 30 20.</p>

      <h2>Hôtel de la Tour: pets not accepted</h2>
      <p>The Hôtel de la Tour, on the harbour at 24 quai Charles-de-Gaulle and run by the Mercier family since 1936, is sometimes described as dog-friendly. Its own website says "We do not accept pets", and the Sanary tourist office lists "Animaux acceptés : non". It is not suitable for a stay with a dog.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>Your dog's weight decides: under 10 kg, the Adonis in the town centre has the lower supplement; above that, only La Farandole publishes a welcome with no weight limit, at €30 per night. In both cases, mention the dog when booking.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the Adonis website applies the 10 kg limit strictly; if your dog is heavier, book elsewhere directly.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The <a href="/en/fiche-bandol">Bandol Dog Beach</a> and the <a href="/en/fiche-six-fours">Brutal Beach in Six-Fours</a> are both under 15 minutes by car, with a <a href="/en/fiche-dogwash-six-fours-les-plages">dog wash in Six-Fours</a> to rinse your dog off after swimming.</p>
